<h3>About General Physics I for Calculus Majors</h3>

<table border="0" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width:1128px">
	<tbody>
		<tr>
			<td style="width:266px"><a href="http://opennj.net/AA00001656/00000" target="_blank"><img alt="General Physics I (Calculus Majprs) Eugene de Silva OTC" src="https://opennj.net/design/aggregations/genphysics_calc/uploads/Physics_Calc_I.jpg" style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); float:left; font-size:17.6px; height:135px; width:250px" /></a></td>
			<td style="width:850px">
			<p>General Physics I for Calculus Majors is the first of two books of a calculus -based -physics course. It provides a rigorous introduction to the fundamentals of Newtonian mechanics. Further topics include oscillatory motion, resonance, mechanical waves, sound, standing waves, and superposition, and Newton&#39;s law of universal gravitation and orbital motion. The course builds upon OpenStax College Physics.</p>

